		(uuid "729559fd-c1ea-4344-98ba-cad9ebc5c3ca")
	)
	(text "PACK WIRES  (welded 4S EVE INR21700-58E)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7cd55707-768c-41d2-a8dc-9420b3ba9024")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n1. CELL_N = gauge VSS (cell 1 negative). GND = system ground, on the far side of RS101.\n2. Kelvin-route SRP/SRN from the RS101 pads; R107/R108/C106 at the IC. RS101 is a 1206 1 W 75 ppm alloy part (P0).\n3. VC taps are separate thin traces from the tap pads J109-J111 and from the J108/J112 pads;\n    VC4 from CELL_P_RAW (before F102) so fuse drop is not read as cell voltage.\n4. TS1-TS4: one wired 10k NTC per cell on J102, J105-J107, taped to the cell at mid-height; insulated sensors only\n    (cans 0-12.6 V above VSS, TS 2.1 V max). PTC, PTCEN, PRES, DISP tied to VSS per datasheet.\n5. VCC fed from FET common drain via R106 (TI R13). PACK sense via R113 10k (TI R15).\n6. BAT fed from CELL_P_RAW (cell top, before F102) via D101 + R105 (TI fig. 9-12).\n7. Diamonds are PWR_FLAGs (ERC only, no part): each sits where its rail is sourced through a passive part.\n8. Q103 buffers BTP_INT onto the shared open-drain IRQ_N (CC2340 DIO11): IRQ_N is low while BTP_INT is high.\n   Keep BTP disabled, or set BTP_POL = 1 with BTP_EN = 1, or IRQ_N is held low (review 4 D-2).\n9. D103 clamps Q102 VGS at 15 V in a hard short. The dev board's C109/D102 inrush options are not on P0.\n10. No wake button: the gauge leaves SHUTDOWN when PACK_P comes up, i.e. when USB is plugged in (TPS25751 dead-battery\n    sink + BQ25756 charging with 3V3 down, USB sheet note 11). Confirm on the dev board.\n11. TP110-TP112 = SMBus pogo pads (SMBC, SMBD, GND) for an EV2400 / BQStudio: golden image and calibration.\n    Only with 3V3 up and U301 held in reset (MCU sheet note 10).\n12. TP106 PACK_P and TP109 GND are factory test pads.\n13. ESD caps (TI): C110+C111 in series across the FET pair (fig. 9-2 C1/C2), C107+C108 across PACK+/PACK- (sec. 9.2.2.1.5).\n14. Second level (TI fig. 9-11): U102 BQ294700 (4.35 V/cell, CD 0.1u = 1-2 s) or the gauge FUSE pin turns Q104 on;\n    F102's heater then blows its fuse, permanently opening the cell top. F102 is also the pack's only overcurrent fuse.\n15. Connect the pack with USB unplugged, PACK- first, then the taps bottom-up, then PACK+: a floating tap can read\n    > 4.35 V, U102 trips after 1-2 s and F102 blows. Gauge data flash: COV Delay 1 s, Min Blow Fuse Voltage 10500 mV."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196.596 248.412 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "89b0cf56-9ded-4344-bef1-affe1323f8fe")
	)
